Job Title: Senior Engineering Manager

Location: Bangalore (Hybrid)

Experience: 12+ years designing/developing software, including 5+ years leading software engineering teams

Department: Engineering / Epic Development

Reports To: Director, Epic Development

Job Summary&nbsp; 

As a Senior Manager, Software Engineering in Epic Development, you will lead multiple technical teams and&nbsp; provide expertise to develop and deliver industry-leading software solutions, tools, and platforms for Epic. &nbsp; You will own outcomes across a cluster of Epic teams (spanning areas such as Epic Core, Epic Operations, Epic&nbsp; Accounting, Epic Infrastructure, Epic Interface, or Epic Policy), leading through a layer of Engineering Managers&nbsp; and Tech Leads rather than managing individual contributors directly. &nbsp; 

You will balance hands-on technical credibility in micro frontend and micro backend (API) architectures with&nbsp; leadership of leaders, ensuring strong execution, engineering quality, and alignment between India-based delivery&nbsp; teams and global Epic product and engineering goals. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

People Leadership & Team Management&nbsp; 

• Recruit and coach high-performing software engineering teams across your area; support skill development&nbsp; and adoption of new technologies, including AI tools. &nbsp; 

• Define expectations for responsible AI usage across multiple teams, use AI to proactively interpret trends in&nbsp; delivery and quality, and share lessons learned across teams. &nbsp; 

• Define and cascade goals so that teams deliver business results aligned to company objectives each year. • Support leaders and teams through change or uncertainty - communicating the benefits of change, addressing&nbsp; concerns, and enabling skill development. &nbsp; 

• Provide input on financial decisions, including team compensation, within established guidelines. • Recruit, retain, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Engineering Managers, Tech Leads, and Senior&nbsp; Software Engineers. &nbsp; 

Technical Leadership & Architecture&nbsp; 

• Provide hands-on technical leadership in micro frontend and microservice-based architectures across the&nbsp; teams you own. &nbsp; 

• Lead architectural decision-making for distributed, modular systems within Epic, in partnership&nbsp; with Epic Architecture. &nbsp; 

• Ensure strong code review practices, technical ownership, and adherence to engineering standards across&nbsp; teams. &nbsp; 

• Drive API scalability, performance, and reliability improvements at a multi-team level. • Support platform modernization and distributed system design across your area of Epic Development. &nbsp; 

Planning, Delivery & Execution

• Collaborate with Product Management, Architecture, and Engineering Leadership to support quarterly&nbsp; planning and produce accurate estimates. &nbsp; 

• Identify and address issues impacting progress across teams; own solutions to operational challenges affecting&nbsp; one or multiple teams; escalate issues and trade-offs to Epic Development leadership to support decisions. • Anticipate potential blockers and monitor progress to proactively enable effective collaboration within and&nbsp; across teams. &nbsp; 

• Maintain metrics, and identify and address blockers or dependencies to ensure continued progress across&nbsp; multiple teams; improve processes and share documentation; share insights with leadership to support capacity&nbsp; planning. &nbsp; 

• Maintain system uptime, limit defects, and ensure production issues are addressed rapidly, with support from&nbsp; technology leadership. &nbsp; 

• Strengthen test automation, CI/CD pipelines, and quality practices consistently across teams operating in&nbsp; Agile Scrum. &nbsp; 

Cross-Functional Collaboration&nbsp; 

• Inform and influence direct reports, peers, and leadership to ensure understanding, alignment, and effective&nbsp; collaboration. &nbsp; 

• Confirm quarterly commitments with support from technology leadership when needed. • Recommend improvements to internal practices and documentation across teams. &nbsp; 

• Communicate clearly with technical and non-technical stakeholders, including global Epic product and&nbsp; engineering counterparts. &nbsp; 

Required Skills & Qualifications&nbsp; 

Must Have (Global Job Framework - Senior Manager level) • 12+ years of experience designing and developing software and/or solutions for internal teams. • 5+ years leading software engineering teams to deliver new features and/or system enhancements, including&nbsp; &nbsp; 

experience leading through Engineering Managers or Tech Leads across more than one team. • Degree in Computer Science, a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. • Advanced knowledge of software development methodologies, programming languages, cloud platforms, and&nbsp; software security. &nbsp; 

• Proven knowledge of software development lifecycle practices and tools such as Jira and Confluence. • Ability to support planning and sizing to ensure accurate estimates across multiple teams. • Ability to address root causes of technical and operational issues. &nbsp; 

• Demonstrated ability to hire, coach, and develop technical teams (not only individual engineers). Epic Engineering - Domain-Specific Must Haves&nbsp; 

• Proven experience leading teams working on micro frontend and microservice architectures. • Strong backend development skills with REST API design and development expertise. • Hands-on experience with: &nbsp; 

◦ C# / . NET&nbsp; 

◦ ReactJS&nbsp; 

◦ TypeScript / JavaScript&nbsp; 

◦ SQL Server&nbsp; 

• Experience working in Agile Scrum environments across multiple squads. &nbsp; 

Preferred / Good to Have&nbsp; 

• Experience with micro frontend frameworks and design patterns at scale. &nbsp; 

• Familiarity with Git, Jira, Confluence, and CI/CD tools (Jenkins, Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions). 

• Experience building cloud-native applications (AWS or Azure). &nbsp; 

• Knowledge of Docker and Kubernetes. &nbsp; 

• Experience in insurance technology or SaaS products. &nbsp; 

• Background scaling teams in globally distributed environments. &nbsp; 

• Prior experience as an Engineering Manager within Epic Development who is ready for multi-team&nbsp; ownership. &nbsp; 

Soft Skills (Very Important for This Role)&nbsp; 

• Ability to lead through other managers, not only through direct execution. &nbsp; 

• Strong coaching and mentoring mindset, including coaching Engineering Managers. • Data-driven decision-making and accountability across multiple teams. &nbsp; 

• Clear communication with diverse, global stakeholders. &nbsp; 

• Adaptability to changing priorities and time zones. &nbsp; 

• Collaborative leadership with timely decision-making, and the courage and compassion to address&nbsp; performance gaps. &nbsp; 

Key Performance Outcomes&nbsp; 

(Aligned to the Global Job Framework's Senior Manager Key Performance Outcomes, to Epic engineering)&nbsp; 

• Engineering teams delivering new features or system enhancements in alignment with the Epic&nbsp; product roadmap; successful outcomes recognized and performance gaps addressed with courage and&nbsp; compassion. &nbsp; 

• Technical solutions recommended and insights shared with technology and product management leaders to&nbsp; ensure team success; team members sharing knowledge to support each other with effective problem solving. • Metrics maintained and blockers or dependencies identified and addressed to ensure continued progress across&nbsp; multiple teams; processes improved and documentation shared; insights shared with leadership to support&nbsp; capacity planning. &nbsp; 

• System uptime maintained, defects limited, and any production issues addressed rapidly with support from&nbsp; technology leadership. &nbsp; 

• Team members and leaders working productively, with gaps addressed with courage and compassion, and&nbsp; building technical skills to ensure continued success. &nbsp;
